libfprint-2-tod1-canvasbio-cb2000 (1.0.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The engine computes cos, sin and atan2 itself (AMD LibM constants), so
    results no longer depend on the C library or the processor; the USB
    interface is claimed without a kernel driver detach; scratch buffers
    are zeroed at allocation.

 -- Kristofer Pagnussat <kristofer.pagnussat@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300

libfprint-2-tod1-canvasbio-cb2000 (1.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A damaged stored print is reported as unreadable instead of as a finger
    that does not match; hardened a distance computed from print data; the
    offline tests run in every package build.

 -- Kristofer Pagnussat <kristofer.pagnussat@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0300

libfprint-2-tod1-canvasbio-cb2000 (1.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The coverage and interrupt status replies are filed by a tag on the
    command table instead of by sequence name; nothing changes on the wire.

 -- Kristofer Pagnussat <kristofer.pagnussat@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:30:00 -0300

libfprint-2-tod1-canvasbio-cb2000 (1.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First release: libfprint TOD module for the CanvasBio CB2000 (2df0:0003),
    matching with an independently written engine that uses the sensor's
    Windows engine as its compatibility target.

 -- Kristofer Pagnussat <kristofer.pagnussat@gmail.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:00:00 -0300
